  "content": {
    "title": "When is Final Four? Dates, schedule for Men's March Madness",
    "text": "Updated March 29, 2026, 10:36 a.m. ETOnce the Men's NCAA Tournament bracket was released on Selection Sunday, the clock began ticking for the 68 teams that made the March Madness field to play out a season-long goal that began back in the summer: winning the national championship.After a handful of upsets and improbable runs, a handful of buzzer beaters and a lot of chalk, the field will soon have its four remaining teams.Two teams have already secured their flights to Indianapolis for the Final Four, with No. 1 Arizona defeating No. 2 Purdue for the West Region title and No. 3 Illinois defeating No. 9 Iowa for the South Region title. The final two spots will be secured from Sunday's Elite Eight games in the East and Midwest regions.Here's what to know on when the Final Four is set to take place:When is the Final Four for men's March Madness?Men's Final Four: Saturday, April 4Men's national championship: Monday, April 6The Final Four of the Men's NCAA Tournament will take place across Saturday, April 4 and Monday, April 6. The national semifinal games will take place on April 4 with tip-off times of 6 p.m. ET and 8:30 p.m. ET. The national championship will tip off at 8:30 p.m. ET on April 6.Where is the Final Four for men's March Madness?Location: Lucas Oil Stadium (Indianapolis)The 2026 men's Final Four will take place at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis. It is the fourth time the venue will host the Final Four, and first time since 2021. Lucas Oil Stadium will also host the 2029 Final Four.The city of Indianapolis also has a noted history of hosting the Men's NCAA Tournament national semifinals and championship games, hosting the Final Four a combined nine times between Market Square Arena (1980), RCA Dome (1991, 1997, 2000, 2006) and Lucas Oil Stadium (2010, 2015, 2021, 2026).Final Four schedule 2026Here's a breakdown of the Final Four schedule for the 2026 NCAA Tournament, including tip-off times and TV channel information:Final FourDate: Saturday, April 4Time: 6 p.m. ET (Game 1) | 8:30 p.m. ET (Game 2)TV channel: TBSStreaming options: March Madness Live app and Sling TVMen's NCAA Tournament national championshipDate: Monday, April 6Time: 8:30 p.m. ETTV channel: TBSStreaming options: March Madness Live app and Sling TVStream Final Four live with Sling TVHow to watch Final Four for men's March MadnessTV channel: TBSStreaming options: March Madness Live app | Sling TVThe Final Four of the Men's NCAA Tournament will be broadcast on TBS. Streaming options include the March Madness Live app (with a TV login) and Sling TV.",
